Description: Restore a Wayland window whose saved ID begins with eight decimal digits.
 Before restoring a window under its saved ID, CreateRestoreSession() replaces an ID saved on X11, the workspace
 number, by a new UUID (Mozilla bug 2059617). It recognized such an ID by ToInteger() succeeding, but ToInteger()
 skips the opening brace of a UUID, reads digits and stops without an error at the first hyphen. A UUID whose first
 group consists of decimal digits only, as about one in 43 random UUIDs does ((10/16)^8), was thus replaced too, so
 that window was added to the session under a new ID instead of being restored, and opened on the current
 workspace. An ID is now kept when it parses as a UUID as a whole and replaced otherwise.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-06
diff --git a/widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp b/widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp
index db3e183..9d5b722 100644
--- a/widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp
+++ b/widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp
@@ -102,12 +102,11 @@ bool nsWindowWayland::CreateRestoreSession(bool aRestoreWindow) {
   }
 
   // If we have old profile / workspace ID or it's empty just replace it by
-  // UUID to avoid protocol error crash (Bug 2059617).
-  nsresult ret = NS_OK;
-  if (!mWorkspaceID.IsEmpty()) {
-    (void)mWorkspaceID.ToInteger(&ret);
-  }
-  if (NS_SUCCEEDED(ret)) {
+  // UUID to avoid protocol error crash (Bug 2059617). Every ID saved for a
+  // Wayland window is a UUID from GenerateWorkspaceID(), while one saved on
+  // X11 is the workspace number, so an ID which is not a UUID is replaced.
+  nsID id;
+  if (!id.Parse(mWorkspaceID)) {
     mWorkspaceID = GenerateWorkspaceID();
     aRestoreWindow = false;
   }
